    "result_text": "All 21 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `Cp11Tests` and the existing `Cp10Tests`, with no regressions.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `householdId` shared-identifier feature for `POST /api/owners`. The `sharesHousehold` acceptance (Cp10) already existed; what was missing was the household identifier itself (Cp11).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` string property to the `Owner` response schema (the generated `OwnerDto` picks it up automatically at build time).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, when `sharesHousehold` is true, it now calls `assignHousehold(owner)` instead of only skipping the duplicate rejection:\n   - `assignHousehold` finds existing owners with the same last name and address (using the existing case/whitespace-insensitive normalization).\n   - If a household exists, it assigns the joining owner **and** the existing member(s) the same `householdId` \u2014 reusing an existing member's id if present, otherwise minting a **stable, deterministic** id via `householdIdFor` (first 16 hex chars of `SHA-256(\"<lastName>|<address>\")`). Determinism means independently created housemates converge on one value.\n   - If no housemate exists, no id is assigned (the owner simply founds a new address).\n\n`OwnerMapper` needed no changes \u2014 MapStruct auto-maps the same-named `householdId` on `Owner` \u2194 `OwnerDto`, so the value is returned in the create/get responses.",
